{"y":1996,"label":"1995–96","coach":"Jim Calhoun","conf":"Big East","confDiv":"Big East 6","confShort":"Big East","w":32,"l":3,"cw":17,"cl":1,"confFinish":"1st in Big East","finish":"sweet16","seed":1,"region":"Southeast","apPre":6,"apHigh":3,"apFinal":3,"srs":26.05,"sos":8.19,"ortg":108.6,"drtg":85.1,"ppg":82.6,"oppg":64.7,"story":{"headline":"Ray Allen's Big East Masterpiece","text":"The 1995–96 Huskies won 23 straight games, went 17–1 in the Big East for a third consecutive regular-season title, and delivered one of the greatest finishes in Big East tournament history. Trailing Georgetown 74–63 with four minutes left in the championship game at Madison Square Garden, UConn closed on a 12–0 run capped by Ray Allen's off-balance winner with 14 seconds to go, 75–74. Allen was named Big East Player of the Year and a consensus first-team All-American, and Calhoun was Big East Coach of the Year. In the NCAA tournament UConn beat Colgate and Eastern Michigan before Mississippi State ended the season 60–55 in the Sweet Sixteen; the NCAA later vacated UConn's 1996 tournament games after two players were ruled ineligible. Allen went fifth overall in the 1996 draft, with Travis Knight (29th) and Sheffer (36th) also selected.","moments":[{"date":"1996-03-09","title":"Ray Allen's winner","text":"UConn closes on a 12–0 run and Ray Allen's floater beats Georgetown 75–74 for the Big East title."},{"date":"1996-03-14","title":"NCAA First Round: W vs Colgate","text":"UConn beat Colgate 68–59 in the NCAA tournament first round at RCA Dome, Indianapolis. (Later vacated by the NCAA.)"},{"date":"1996-03-16","title":"NCAA Second Round: W vs Eastern Michigan","text":"UConn beat Eastern Michigan 95–81 in the NCAA tournament second round at RCA Dome, Indianapolis. (Later vacated by the NCAA.)"},{"date":"1996-03-22","title":"NCAA Sweet Sixteen: L vs Mississippi State","text":"UConn lost to Mississippi State 55–60 in the NCAA tournament sweet sixteen at Rupp Arena, Lexington, Kentucky. (Later vacated by the NCAA.)"}],"honors":["Big East 6 Division regular-season champions","Big East tournament champions","Ray Allen – Consensus first-team All-American","Ray Allen – UPI College Player of the Year","Ray Allen – Big East Player of the Year","Jim Calhoun – Big East Coach of the Year","Ray Allen – First-team All-Big East"],"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1995%E2%80%9396_Connecticut_Huskies_men's_basketball_team","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UConn_Huskies_men%27s_basketball","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Calhoun","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ray_Allen"]},"roster":[{"pid":"ray-allen-1","name":"Ray Allen","num":"34","cls":"JR","pos":"G","ht":"6-5","wt":205,"home":"Dalzell, SC","photo":"assets/players/ray-allen-1.jpg?v=9ea25de4","photoWide":true,"pg":{"g":35,"gs":35,"mp":34.7,"pts":23.4,"trb":6.5,"ast":3.3,"stl":1.7,"blk":0.5,"tov":2.3,"fg_pct":0.472,"fg3_pct":0.466,"ft_pct":0.81,"orb":2.3,"pf":1.3},"tot":{"mp":1215,"fg":292,"fga":618,"fg3":115,"fg3a":247,"ft":119,"fta":147,"orb":81,"drb":147,"trb":228,"ast":117,"stl":60,"blk":18,"tov":82,"pf":46,"pts":818,"g":35},"adv":{"per":null,"ts_pct":0.595,"efg_pct":0.566,"usg_pct":null,"ast_pct":null,"trb_pct":null,"stl_pct":null,"blk_pct":null,"ws":8.3,"ws_per_40":0.274,"bpm":null,"obpm":null,"dbpm":null},"verified":["record_book"]},{"pid":"doron-sheffer-1","name":"Doron Sheffer","num":"11","cls":"JR","pos":"G","ht":"6-5","wt":185,"home":"Ramat Efal, Israel","photo":"assets/players/doron-sheffer-1.jpg?v=6f798b04","photoWide":true,"pg":{"g":35,"gs":35,"mp":31.9,"pts":16.0,"trb":4.8,"ast":6.1,"stl":1.9,"blk":0.4,"tov":3.1,"fg_pct":0.43,"fg3_pct":0.406,"ft_pct":0.849,"orb":1.4,"pf":1.9},"tot":{"mp":1116,"fg":182,"fga":423,"fg3":95,"fg3a":234,"ft":101,"fta":119,"orb":48,"drb":121,"trb":169,"ast":212,"stl":65,"blk":13,"tov":108,"pf":68,"pts":560,"g":35},"adv":{"per":null,"ts_pct":0.584,"efg_pct":0.543,"usg_pct":null,"ast_pct":null,"trb_pct":null,"stl_pct":null,"blk_pct":null,"ws":6.6,"ws_per_40":0.236,"bp